      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Deepdives\n\nUrl shortener should be\n- fast\n- unique\n- short (5-7 chars) ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Deepdives\n\nUrl shortener should be\n- fast\n- unique\n- short (5-7 chars) ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "_4m4OfvHQ7hQ96n8GunXx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1607.3758682088628,
      "y": 111.13799662904341,
      "width": 8,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aW",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 187865958,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1037434746,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783060900869,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WL6nL8zpXZU-CmjamZZr7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1594.4958856151952,
      "y": 109.21749589281262,
      "width": 1557.3590087890625,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aX",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1927723942,
      "version": 2141,
      "versionNonce": 836899706,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783062014094,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Solutions\n1. prefix of long url, take 5-7 chars from start/end and use that as short code(www.bitly.com/facebook)\n    - Poor approach, lots of duplication, tons of url start with same prefix. Never Use it\n2. Random number generator\n    - Given 1B urls, so our number should be between 1-1B ~ 10^9 or 10chars, can't use directly, encode it\n    - base62 encode it 0-9, A-Z, a-z = total 62 options for a single digit\n    - 62^6(avg code length) = 56B combinations - good number of options but what about collisions\n    - Birthday Paradox applied here i.e. what is the probab that a number randomly generated b/w 1-56B when calculated a billion times what will be the collison\n    - 880k collisions - How to fix?\n    - Before saving to the DB check if this code already exists? i.e. just introduce another read.\n3. Hash the long url\n    - md5/sha256/murmurhash(long url) -> hash -> base62(hash)[:6] i.e. just take first 6 chars\n    - Chances of collision same as above, need to check DB before saving.\n4. Counter\n    - Increment a counter from 1 - 56B -> base62 encode it.\n    - No need for DB lookup now.\n    - Security concern - Predictability is very high as hackers can randomly generate nos encode it know what url customer is using.\n    - Our competitors can exactly know from where we started and till what we've generated so far and scrape all our urls.\n        - Solution could be warning to our customers \"Don't shorten private urls\"\n        - Rate Limiting.\n    - Proper solution to this problem is bijective function - the issue a 1-1 matching given a number\n        - squids.org library for this\n        - Give your counter to this lib it will generate a 5-7 char code for you so that it can never be increased incremently!.\n    ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Solutions\n1. prefix of long url, take 5-7 chars from start/end and use that as short code(www.bitly.com/facebook)\n    - Poor approach, lots of duplication, tons of url start with same prefix. Never Use it\n2. Random number generator\n    - Given 1B urls, so our number should be between 1-1B ~ 10^9 or 10chars, can't use directly, encode it\n    - base62 encode it 0-9, A-Z, a-z = total 62 options for a single digit\n    - 62^6(avg code length) = 56B combinations - good number of options but what about collisions\n    - Birthday Paradox applied here i.e. what is the probab that a number randomly generated b/w 1-56B when calculated a billion times what will be the collison\n    - 880k collisions - How to fix?\n    - Before saving to the DB check if this code already exists? i.e. just introduce another read.\n3. Hash the long url\n    - md5/sha256/murmurhash(long url) -> hash -> base62(hash)[:6] i.e. just take first 6 chars\n    - Chances of collision same as above, need to check DB before saving.\n4. Counter\n    - Increment a counter from 1 - 56B -> base62 encode it.\n    - No need for DB lookup now.\n    - Security concern - Predictability is very high as hackers can randomly generate nos encode it know what url customer is using.\n    - Our competitors can exactly know from where we started and till what we've generated so far and scrape all our urls.\n        - Solution could be warning to our customers \"Don't shorten private urls\"\n        - Rate Limiting.\n    - Proper solution to this problem is bijective function - the issue a 1-1 matching given a number\n        - squids.org library for this\n        - Give your counter to this lib it will generate a 5-7 char code for you so that it can never be increased incremently!.\n    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
