    {
      "id": "YWPoZ7LOUvpzb4X2-cN3B",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1371.0351664816296,
      "y": 2273.5611564461033,
      "width": 1468.0191650390625,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b07",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 871995642,
      "version": 825,
      "versionNonce": 1005944358,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783063274576,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Modern Hardware is mostly auto-scaling depending on traffic it up-scales and down-scales automatically.\n- Problem with Write Service, if we have multiple write service how do we sync their counters\n- We use INCR Redis increment call to maintain a common counter\n- Instead of reaching out for Global counter for each create request we request 1000 counter together same for other read service i.e. 1001 - 2000\n  this way we don't have to reach out to Global Counter and make our system slow\n- Even if some service crashes, so what we loose 1000 counts but we have 56B to our account np.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Modern Hardware is mostly auto-scaling depending on traffic it up-scales and down-scales automatically.\n- Problem with Write Service, if we have multiple write service how do we sync their counters\n- We use INCR Redis increment call to maintain a common counter\n- Instead of reaching out for Global counter for each create request we request 1000 counter together same for other read service i.e. 1001 - 2000\n  this way we don't have to reach out to Global Counter and make our system slow\n- Even if some service crashes, so what we loose 1000 counts but we have 56B to our account np.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
